-- title:
--   Reduction of Φ modulo p equals Φ₀
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring carrying an algebra structure over $\mathbf Z/p$ and complete for the $(p)$-adic topology, $r$ a natural number, and $H_1$ a Honda system for the element $p\in\mathcal O$ on the module $\mathcal O^{r}$, i.e. a pair of $\mathcal O$-linear maps $F,V$ with $FV=VF=p$ together with a submodule $L$ satisfying the usual conditions. Let $G$ be a family of commutative rings $G_v$ with Hopf algebra structures over $\mathbf Z/p$, $s_v:G_{v+1}\to G_v$ a family of coalgebra algebra maps, and $\pi_v:\mathcal O^{r}\to D(G_v)$ additive maps into the Dieudonné modules. Let $\mathcal S$ be a split-coordinates datum for $(p,r,H_1,G,s,\pi)$ — with dimension $d$, heights $h^c,h^e$, connected and étale factors $G^c_v,G^e_v$ with their transition maps, maps $q^c_v$, $\pi^e_v$, $\sigma_v$, $\Theta_v$, a $d$-dimensional formal group law $\Phi_0$ over $\mathbf Z/p$, presentations $\kappa_v:(\mathbf Z/p)[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to G^c_v$, and the auxiliary lifted data $E_v$, $\hat c$, $M^c$, $M^{et}$, $\alpha$, $\bar a$ — and assume $\mathcal S$ is `Lawful`, i.e. satisfies the full list of axioms of that structure (local finite connected factors of rank $p^{vh^c}$, reduced formally unramified étale factors of rank $p^{vh^e}$, $h^c+h^e=r$, bijectivity of $\Theta_v$, surjectivity of $\kappa_v$ with kernel generated by the $p^v$-division series of $\Phi_0$, the comultiplication formula for $\kappa_v(X_i)$, and the stated compatibilities; summarised here). Let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$ (a $d$-tuple of power series in two sets of $d$ variables with vanishing constant term, linear coefficients $X_i+Y_i$, and associativity). Assume: for every commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $g$ that is finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module and all $x,y\in g^{d}$ with every coordinate nilpotent, there are a level $v$ and $\mathbf Z/p$-algebra maps $f_x,f_y:G^c_v\to (\mathbf Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O} g$ with $f_x(\kappa_v(X_j))=1\otimes x_j$ and $f_y(\kappa_v(X_j))=1\otimes y_j$ for all $j$, whose convolution product satisfies $(f_x\ast f_y)(\kappa_v(X_i))=1\otimes \Phi_i(x,y)$ for all $i$, the right-hand side being the $(p)$-adic evaluation of the $i$-th series of $\Phi$ at the $2d$-tuple $(x,y)$. Then the coefficientwise reduction of $\Phi$ along $\mathcal O\to\mathbf Z/p$ equals $\Phi_0$.
--
--   This is the coordinate form of the assertion that a formal group law over $\mathcal O$ whose addition is computed by the group law of the connected factors $G^c_v$ has special fibre the law $\Phi_0$ attached to the connected–étale splitting, as in Fontaine's analysis of $p$-divisible groups and Honda systems over local rings. It is used in [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_mvFormalGroup_cocycle_of_splitCoordinates`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_mvFormalGroup_cocycle_of_splitCoordinates), where a lift of the formal group attached to a Honda system is produced together with its cocycle data.
